    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Each morning, five polite policewomen Anna, Bea, Clara, Dana and Ella walk to the police station in a line in exactly this order. On the way to the changing room on the far end of the building there are 8 doors. Each door is held open by the first policewoman in the line, who walks at the end of the line after the others have passed. Who opens the last door?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "Anna"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "Bea"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "Clara"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "Dana"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "Ella"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Follow the line",
        "body": "The first door is opened by Anna, who then goes to the back: the order becomes Bea, Clara, Dana, Ella, Anna. So the doors are opened in the cyclic order Anna, Bea, Clara, Dana, Ella, Anna, Bea, Clara. Door 8 is opened by Clara.\n\n**Answer: (C) Clara**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Remainders",
        "body": "The women take turns in a cycle of 5. Door 8 is the $8 - 5 = 3$rd in the second round, i.e. the third woman: Clara.\n\n**Answer: (C) Clara**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "patterns",
      "logic"
    ],
