      {
        "title": "Arcs between the vertices",
        "body": "All vertices lie on a circle. A triangle inscribed in a circle is equilateral exactly when its vertices split the circle into three equal arcs, i.e. when consecutive vertices of the triangle are $\\frac{2012}{3}$ steps apart along the polygon. But 2012 is not divisible by 3 ($2+0+1+2 = 5$), so there is no such triangle. The number is 0, which is not among (A)–(D).\n\n**Answer: (E) other answer**"
