      "number": 21,
      "url": "https://api.mathkangaroo.ca/api/v1/media/2012/2012gr1112e.pdf"
    },
    "grade": "11-12",
    "points": 5,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "We are given a right-angled triangle with sides of length $a$, $b$ and $c$. What is the radius $r$ of the inscribed semicircle shown in the figure?",
    "image": "qimages/kangaroo/ca-2012-g1112/q21.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$\\frac{a(c-a)}{2b}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$\\frac{ab}{a+b+c}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$\\frac{ab}{b+c}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$\\frac{2ab}{a+b+c}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$\\frac{ab}{a+c}$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Split the area",
        "body": "The centre $O$ of the semicircle lies on $b$, at distance $r$ from the lines of $a$ and $c$ (the semicircle touches $a$ and $c$). Joining $O$ to the vertex where $a$ and $c$ meet splits the triangle into two triangles with bases $a$ and $c$, both with height $r$:\n\n$$\\frac{ab}{2} = \\frac{ar}{2} + \\frac{cr}{2} \\implies r = \\frac{ab}{a+c}.$$\n\n**Answer: (E)**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Similar triangles",
        "body": "Let the semicircle touch $c$ at $T$. The triangle formed by the centre $O$, $T$ and the vertex where $b$ meets $c$ is similar to the whole triangle, giving $\\frac{r}{a} = \\frac{b - r}{c}$. So $cr = ab - ar$ and $r = \\frac{ab}{a + c}$. (Check with $a = 3, b = 4, c = 5$: $r = \\frac{12}{8} = 1.5$, and the distance from $(1.5, 0)$ to $3x + 4y = 12$ is $\\frac{7.5}{5} = 1.5$. ✓)\n\n**Answer: (E)**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "geometry",
      "algebra"
    ],
