    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "How many solutions does the system of equations have?\n\n$$|x| + |y| = 1,\\qquad x^2 - y^2 = 1$$",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "1"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "8"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "0"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Factor the difference of squares",
        "body": "$x^2 - y^2 = |x|^2 - |y|^2 = (|x| - |y|)(|x| + |y|) = |x| - |y|$, using the first equation. So $|x| - |y| = 1$ and $|x| + |y| = 1$, giving $|x| = 1$, $|y| = 0$. The solutions are $(1, 0)$ and $(-1, 0)$: two solutions.\n\n**Answer: (B) 2**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Graphs",
        "body": "$|x| + |y| = 1$ is a square with vertices $(\\pm1, 0)$, $(0, \\pm1)$. The hyperbola $x^2 - y^2 = 1$ has vertices $(\\pm1, 0)$ and otherwise lies in $|x| > 1$, outside the square. They meet only at $(1,0)$ and $(-1,0)$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 2**"
      }
    ],
